## Cal.com link conventions

### The canonical booking URLs

Each motion routes to its own Cal.com event type so calendar attribution stays clean and the post-book confirmation can be tailored per motion.

| Page | Cal.com path | Event type name |
|---|---|---|
| versafilecanada.com | `https://cal.com/jonmc/versafile-intro` | "VersaFile — 15-min intro" |
| plinkoenergy.com | `https://cal.com/jonmc/plinko-energy-intro` | "Plinko Energy — 15-min intro" |
| tryplinko.com | `https://cal.com/jonmc/plinko-msp-intro` | "Plinko MSP — 15-min intro" |
| dfyplinko.com | `https://cal.com/jonmc/plinko-msp-dfy-intro` | "Plinko DFY — 15-min intro" |

### UTM and attribution enrichment

Every Cal.com link gets query parameters appended at click-time by the page's JavaScript. The parameters are:

- `utm_source`, `utm_medium`, `utm_campaign`, `utm_term`, `utm_content` — passed through from the landing URL
- `source_domain` — set by the page (e.g., `versafilecanada.com`)
- `motion` — set by the page (e.g., `versafile`, `plinko-energy`, `plinko-msp-try`, `plinko-msp-dfy`)

These flow to Cal.com as booking metadata, then forward via webhook to n8n for CRM routing.

### Button label rules

The button text varies per page voice but follows a shared pattern: a specific, named next step, not a generic verb.

| Page | Primary button label |
|---|---|
| versafilecanada.com | "Book a 15-minute intro call" |
| plinkoenergy.com | "Book a 15-minute intro call" |
| tryplinko.com | "Grab a 15-minute intro call" |
| dfyplinko.com | "Book your 15-minute fit call" |

Avoid: "Get in touch", "Contact us", "Let's talk", "Learn more", "Sign up", "Get started."
These are vague verbs. Named, time-bounded commitments ("15-minute intro") convert better because the buyer knows exactly what they're committing to.

