## CTA placement on each page

### Rule of three

Every page has exactly three Cal.com CTA instances, at predictable positions:

1. **Hero block** — immediately under the subheadline. The scroll-skippers who already know they want a call need this at the top.
2. **Mid-page** — after the proof or process section, once the buyer has seen evidence. This is for the "convinced at third of the way down" buyer.
3. **Final CTA section** — the dedicated closing block, above the footer. For the bottom-reader who scrolled the whole page.

Never more than three. Each extra Cal.com button below three adds clutter, not conversions.

### The form placement

The contact form goes directly above the final CTA section. Why: the final CTA is the last Cal.com touch; the form is the "I'm not ready to book but I want to signal interest" fallback. Buyers who resisted the first two Cal.com buttons can still convert via form before they hit the third.

