## Risk reversal language

Every Cal.com CTA is accompanied by a risk-reversal phrase. The goal: make the click feel zero-cost.

Approved risk-reversal phrases per page:

**versafilecanada.com:** "No pressure. No mandatory demo. If we're not the right fit, we'll tell you."

**plinkoenergy.com:** "Worst case, one honest opinion on the M-Files question."

**tryplinko.com:** "No pitch deck. If it's a waste of your time, we'll tell you in the first five minutes."

**dfyplinko.com:** "No pitch deck. If this isn't right for your MSP, we'll tell you what we'd recommend instead."

Risk-reversal sits next to the button, not as a separate paragraph. It's a single sentence that reduces the psychological cost of clicking.

