## UTM parameter conventions

We use a consistent UTM taxonomy across all outreach so n8n can attribute back to the right campaign.

### Standard UTM values

| Parameter | Values we use |
|---|---|
| `utm_source` | `smartlead`, `heyreach`, `linkedin`, `referral`, `direct` |
| `utm_medium` | `cold_email`, `inmail`, `connection_msg`, `reply`, `organic` |
| `utm_campaign` | Campaign name from Smartlead/HeyReach (e.g., `vf-t1-records`, `pl-t2-msp-ops`) |
| `utm_term` | Trigger signal if any (e.g., `hiring-records-manager`, `compliance-deadline-q3`) |
| `utm_content` | Which email variant in the sequence (e.g., `step-1`, `step-3-followup`) |

### Capture and persistence

On page load, the JavaScript:
1. Reads all `utm_*` params from `window.location.search`
2. Persists them to `sessionStorage` with a `cw_utm_` prefix (prevents collision)
3. Appends them to every Cal.com link on click
4. Includes them in the form submit POST body

If a buyer lands without UTMs (direct traffic or typed URL), `utm_source=direct` is set as default.

